# Deploy after security work

When adding or changing **security** (headers, CSP, auth, cookies, secrets handling, XSS/safe hrefs, Prisma/server-only, rate limits, API hardening, etc.):

1. Stage only intentional files — **never** commit `.env` or real secrets.
2. Run `git commit` with a clear message (e.g. `security: …`).
3. Run `git push origin main` so **Vercel** rebuilds the live site.

If `git push` fails (auth/network), report the error and what remains to do locally.

Skip auto-push only if the user explicitly asks to hold commits or review first.
